/// One private callee PER DOOR, plus a public control.
///
/// `private` is written out on every one of them and is load-bearing: Q7 makes
/// a top-level declaration PUBLIC by default, so a visibility probe that leaves
/// the keyword off tests nothing at all.
namespace VisibilityValueGate::Vault;

/// DOOR 5a -- named by a written qualified path in value position.  This shape
/// resolves through `resolve_module_qualified_symbol`, the same symbol the CALL
/// form of the path resolves through, so the two spellings cannot disagree
/// about which function they name.
private function tapped() -> i32 { return 5; }

/// DOOR 5b -- named bare in value position.  The leaf is unique program-wide,
/// so the lookup that answers it (`lookup_func_type`) is keyed on the bare name
/// and carries no owner; the gate has to resolve the leaf against the module
/// that WROTE the reference before it has an owner to judge.
private function latched() -> i32 { return 6; }

/// CONTROL: a genuinely public sibling, taken as a value both ways.
public function offered() -> i32 { return 3; }
